                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "78deb464-9fc5-354c-905f-85a51425783d",
                        "entry_id": "7604b248-cc0a-3a1d-a2ff-911928510c75",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A type of Ancient Greek pottery wine jug."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9342d70c-429e-42d9-83cb-dcf9b45c423f",
                                "sense_id": "78deb464-9fc5-354c-905f-85a51425783d",
                                "text": "These two head oenochoae were buried with the kotyle by the Brygos painter (22. 8), B.S.A. xiv, pl. xiv, and the Red Figure kylix (22. 7), ibid. pl. xiii. b."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3e6c073-96da-4c34-9a36-22c4cd1bfe18",
                                "sense_id": "78deb464-9fc5-354c-905f-85a51425783d",
                                "text": "In contact with the upper part of the jar was a dish with rodent or bird bones and two oenochoae, all protected by big blocks of schist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "95c267d7-1cca-463c-b7f8-c67ce829465f",
                                "sense_id": "78deb464-9fc5-354c-905f-85a51425783d",
                                "text": "As we have seen above, Black-on-Red Cypriot trefoil oenochoae together with objects from the Syropalestinian area had started arriving in Crete already before the middle of the 8 cent. B.C."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "827214cd-d676-45a2-91f8-e41b38f82602",
                                "sense_id": "78deb464-9fc5-354c-905f-85a51425783d",
                                "text": "In the tondo of a cup in the Louvre we see a young slave, a pais, dip an oenochoe into a garlanded krater; he is holding a cup in the other hand and is about to serve drinks (fig. 20)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b63004e-a9ae-4794-a7b7-396c09747f3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7604b248-cc0a-3a1d-a2ff-911928510c75",
